.TH chown "" "Command"
.SH NAME
chown \- change the owner of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBchown \fIowner file ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
chown -- change the owner of files
Usage:	chown owner file ...
.HE
.B chown
changes the owner of each
.I file
to
.IR owner .
.I owner
may be given as a user name, looked up in
.BR /etc/passwd ,
or as a plain decimal user identifier.
The group of each
.I file
is left unchanged.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 16n
\fB/etc/passwd\fR	user name to user-id lookup
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chgrp ,
.B chmod
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B chown
exits with status 2 if
.I owner
is not a valid user name, or if any
.I file
could not be changed (in which case it also prints the reason for
that file and continues with the rest).
